  "market": [
    {
      "id": "https://wan-ifra.org/?p=120869",
      "title": "The Integrity Dividend: The Value of Knowing",
      "link": "https://wan-ifra.org/2026/09/the-integrity-dividend-the-value-of-knowing/",
      "published": "Mon, 28 Sep 2026 08:09:41 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>Disinformation now carries an estimated annual cost of US$350–510 billion worldwide – which is why governments, platforms and media organisations should strengthen oversight, enforcement and rigour, argues this joint op ed that marks both World News Day and the International Day for Universal Access to Information.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org/2026/09/the-integrity-dividend-the-value-of-knowing/\">The Integrity Dividend: The Value of Knowing</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org\">WAN-IFRA</a>.</p>",
      "source": "WAN-IFRA"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://wan-ifra.org/?p=121049",
      "title": "Truth in an AI World",
      "link": "https://wan-ifra.org/2026/09/truth-in-an-ai-world/",
      "published": "Sun, 27 Sep 2026 15:22:55 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>\"As the tools for manufacturing fiction keep improving, the case for championing the people committed to fact only grows stronger.\" On World News Day, News Corp Australasia's  Executive Chairman Michael Miller, makes the case for support of local news.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org/2026/09/truth-in-an-ai-world/\">Truth in an AI World</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org\">WAN-IFRA</a>.</p>",
      "source": "WAN-IFRA"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://wan-ifra.org/?p=121032",
      "title": "Things I learned from my daughters, a central bank investigation, and a box of watermelon gum",
      "link": "https://wan-ifra.org/2026/09/things-i-learned-from-my-daughters-a-central-bank-investigation-and-a-box-of-watermelon-gum/",
      "published": "Sun, 27 Sep 2026 07:23:16 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>‘Producing journalism is not enough if we fail to distribute it.’ – Alia Ibrahim, co-founder and CEO of independent Lebanese news outlet Daraj, unlocks the generational key to storytelling in a time of transition, for World News Day 2026.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org/2026/09/things-i-learned-from-my-daughters-a-central-bank-investigation-and-a-box-of-watermelon-gum/\">Things I learned from my daughters, a central bank investigation, and a box of watermelon gum</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org\">WAN-IFRA</a>.</p>",
      "source": "WAN-IFRA"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://wan-ifra.org/?p=120950",
      "title": "Journalism & Our Chaotic World’s Future",
      "link": "https://wan-ifra.org/2026/09/journalism-our-chaotic-worlds-future/",
      "published": "Sat, 26 Sep 2026 09:51:26 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>\"We may have to change our form, the way we function and the way we reach audiences but we cannot abandon our purpose.\" – Tina Brown and Branko Brkic exhort journalists to \"to keep the light of shared reality on,\" this World News Day.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org/2026/09/journalism-our-chaotic-worlds-future/\">Journalism &#038; Our Chaotic World’s Future</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org\">WAN-IFRA</a>.</p>",
      "source": "WAN-IFRA"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://wan-ifra.org/?p=120916",
      "title": "Dystopia, Inc: Would you like your news with or without hallucinations?",
      "link": "https://wan-ifra.org/2026/09/dystopia-inc-would-you-like-your-news-with-or-without-hallucinations/",
      "published": "Sat, 26 Sep 2026 06:20:53 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>\"Defending truth and facts costs money and requires values.\" – Phil Chetwynd shares how journalists put themselves at great risk, at incredible cost, to bear witness – sometimes to catastrophes in remote areas of the planet, where there is no Internet – to events that AI can only summarise. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org/2026/09/dystopia-inc-would-you-like-your-news-with-or-without-hallucinations/\">Dystopia, Inc: Would you like your news with or without hallucinations?</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org\">WAN-IFRA</a>.</p>",
      "source": "WAN-IFRA"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://wan-ifra.org/?p=121023",
      "title": "World News Day: 21 Great Op-Eds on Why Journalism Matters",
